WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.798
An airway reopening sounds like relief. On the scale of

00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:07.408
an epithelial monolayer, the arriving air–liquid

00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:10.017
interface can be an injury event.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.335
The machine keeping a patient breathing can also expose

00:00:21.335 --> 00:00:23.925
delicate airway cells to damaging forces.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.065
We modelled one mechanical event in cultured rat

00:00:35.065 --> 00:00:38.680
alveolar epithelial cells: a single air bubble passing

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.035
over a monolayer.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.401
We used a parallel-plate chamber, fluorescence

00:00:49.401 --> 00:00:52.844
live-dead staining, and microscopy to examine what

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:54.812
happened after bubble propagation.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.161
Our experiment tested whether pretreatment with

00:01:05.161 --> 00:01:08.254
dexamethasone or trans-dehydroandrosterone could change

00:01:08.254 --> 00:01:11.347
the cells' susceptibility before exposure.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:19.679
In the untreated bubble-exposed group, 54.7 percent of

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.379
cells were dead. With dexamethasone pretreatment, it

00:01:23.379 --> 00:01:24.965
was 15.1 percent.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.927
With transdehydroandrosterone, cell death was 16.1

00:01:35.927 --> 00:01:41.143
percent. These were rat L2 cultures, exposed to a

00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:42.881
simulated airway-reopening event.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.066
The comparison warrants investigating cellular

00:01:50.066 --> 00:01:54.251
mechanics and prevention. It does not establish a

00:01:54.251 --> 00:01:56.866
clinical treatment for mechanically ventilated

00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:57.389
patients.
